<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10298" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-grex</span></b> , grĕgis,
			adj. (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of the same herd</i> or <i>flock</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equinis armentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, p. 194, 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 2</span></i>
			 dub. (al. congregatae).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In gen., <i>collected
				in flocks</i> or <i>multitudes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">catervas, Auct. Pervig. Ven. 43: vulgo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 10, 21</span></i>
			.—With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comessationibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Poen. 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>close, intimate</i>:
			aliquem congrege nexu tenere, Prud. contra <i><span class="en">Symm. 2,
			634</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
